<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Flowchart diagram illustrating cohort selection of new-onset diabetes patients from 2018 to 2020, exclusion due to conditions or missing data, and final division into nonstatin \(N equals 146\) and statin \(N equals 458\) groups for analysis.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Bar graph \(panel A\) and line graph \(panel B\) comparing HbA1c changes between statin and nonstatin groups over 6, 12, 24, 36, and 60 months; greater reduction observed in nonstatin group at 6 months with significant p-value, while differences at later time points are not statistically significant. Panel B shows both groups\220 mean HbA1c decreasing over time with similar levels after 12 months.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Kaplan-Meier survival curve comparing statin and nonstatin groups for survival free of major adverse cardiovascular events over a 100-month follow-up, with statin group showing higher survival; log-rank test p-value is 0.017. A risk table below displays the number of individuals at risk at intervals for each group.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Multivariate Cox regression forest plot showing hazard ratios with ninety-five percent confidence intervals for group, age, CAD, BMI, and LDL-C. Group is statistically significant with a hazard ratio of zero point forty-one, confidence interval zero point twenty-one to zero point eighty-three, and p-value zero point zero one three.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
